      "sentence_id": 18,
      "text": "5. Respondent No. 2 is represented by his counsel and does not oppose the compromise.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 1995,
      "end": 2081,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 19,
      "text": "6. In view of the aforesaid report of the learned Judicial Magistrate Ist Class, Faridabad, and in view of the decision of the Hon'ble Supreme Court in \"Gian Singh Vs. State of Punjab and another\",\n2012(4) RCR (Criminal) 543 and \"Narinder Singh and Others Vs. State of Punjab and Another\",\n(2014) 6 SCC 466, this Court is of the opinion that no useful purpose can be served by keeping with the criminal proceedings pending, since the complainant- respondent No. 2 has himself compromised the dispute with the petitioners/ accused persons.",
